  body: "# Purpose and evidence in deprivation of income\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe captured
    guidance links deprivation of income to securing or increasing benefit, requires the benefit purpose
    to be significant and calls for consideration of all facts rather than assuming purpose from disposal
    alone.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nThe chapter also mentions ESA in these passages; this batch establishes
    no ESA rule and retains its JSA/IS focus. Income already received is treated separately, enforceable
    immediately repayable debt has a qualification, and each new claim requires a fresh decision. Missing
    income is not proof of fraud or intent.\n\n## Inspected source passages\n\n- [DMG 28576, PDF page
    137](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69a16975f534e7e99adaea96/dmg-ch-28.pdf#page=137)
    — DMG Vol 5 Ch 28: Income other than earnings.\n- [DMG 28577, PDF page 137](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69a16975f534e7e99adaea96/dmg-ch-28.pdf#page=137)
    — DMG Vol 5 Ch 28: Income other than earnings.\n- [DMG 28581, PDF page 138](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69a16975f534e7e99adaea96/dmg-ch-28.pdf#page=138)
    — DMG Vol 5 Ch 28: Income other than earnings.\n- [DMG 28582, PDF page 138](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69a16975f534e7e99adaea96/dmg-ch-28.pdf#page=138)
    — DMG Vol 5 Ch 28: Income other than earnings.\n- [DMG 28589, PDF page 139](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69a16975f534e7e99adaea96/dmg-ch-28.pdf#page=139)
    — DMG Vol 5 Ch 28: Income other than earnings.\n- [DMG 28590, PDF page 139](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69a16975f534e7e99adaea96/dmg-ch-28.pdf#page=139)
    — DMG Vol 5 Ch 28: Income other than earnings.\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\nModel-assisted
    interpretation of selected passages in the 15 September 2026 frozen source snapshot. Specialist review
    is required. Source acquisition, source revision, legal effective dates and this record’s authoring
    time are separate.\n\nThis is an independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document,
    individual advice, an entitlement decision or an executable rule. Machine-extracted text may alter
    reading order, footnotes and characters. No PDF visual inspection, whole-chapter coverage or behavioural
    evaluation pass is claimed by this record.\n\n- `dmg-vol5-ch28`: PDF SHA-256 `bcaea58ee40a9dca60a21b0f79c525a1f15e95c6b8315d6aaa73f0f53dd5460f`;
    extracted pages SHA-256 `f7e554c1af4c7d8b915524f441c1680c5bea7429ac8fff9fd18bc0c925f25c31`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/dmg-evidence-assessment
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The source lists explanation, timing, knowledge and likelihood of a claim as facts to
      consider when assessing purpose, rather than prescribing an automatic inference.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol5-ch28/0139
      quote: "28590 It is unlikely that there will be direct evidence that a deprivation was for the purpose
        of getting\nbenefit. Decide on a person's reasons for disposing of an income after considering
        all the facts of the\ncase. These may include\n\n\n1. the person's explanations\n\n\n2. the timing
        of the disposal\n\n\n3. the claimant's knowledge of the benefit system\n\n\n4. the likelihood
        of a benefit claim at the time of the deprivation."
      locator: DMG 28590
